// Source: common.md "unary operators": `a * -1` reads as `(a*) - 1`, a
// dereference, whatever the spacing; spacing that suggests multiplication is
// an error. Upstream emits Cpp1 that dereferences `a`.
// expect-error: this '*' is a postfix dereference of the operand before it, not a binary '*'
main: () = {
    a := 6;
    b := a * -1;
    _ = b;
}
